WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:03.780
It's been 22 years

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.980
since the events in the first movie

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.370
and that means anyone younger than 22 in
a world that we're creating

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.690
has never lived in a world where
dinosaurs didn't exist.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:19.039
They're coming into this with this idea
the dinosaurs are not really that fascinating.

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:22.600
(Corporate felt genetic motification would up the 'wow' factor.)

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.980
(They're dinosaurs 'wow' enough.)

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.510
What does Jurassic World need to do to build a bigger attendance?

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.300
They need to make is bigger, faster, more scary.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:32.800
(That was awesome!)

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.420
The character that I play, Claire, she runs
the park. And she's someone who is very

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.329
disconnected from her own humanity

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:42.400
because in the quest for profit she
makes some disastrous mistakes.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.079
(You just went a made a new dinosaur?)

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:46.500
(Probably not a good idea.)

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.400
(Screaming)

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.809
We shot this movie for IMAX. And so our aspect ratio is the native ratio

00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:57.920
of all the digital IMAX screens in the
world

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.289
So when you see our film the whole thing
takes up the entire screen.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:04.900
It's a pretty stunning experience. You really
do feel the difference.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.900
(You got 20,000 people.)

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.200
(You got no more boats. You don't have enough guns.)

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.000
There's so many sequences in this, that I'm excited to see especially in IMAX.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The Mosasaurus, the underwater stuff, the
'raptor motorcycle sequence

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.200
I think that's going to be pretty great. (If we do this, if we do this my way.)

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.500
Basically, everything! It's just such an iconic
franchise and there are so many people that love

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.220
it so much so it's been quite the honor
to be a part of it.

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:32.200
(We're talking about an animal here.)

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.900
(A highly intelligent animal.) It's crazy like there
were so many moments

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:40.100
on set where all of us felt like we're
all kids in our backyard making a

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.000
dinosaur movie. Like this is such a wish fulfillment for

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.600
someone who saw the original film. It was just an enormous blast.

